  introNarrationText: Ingenuity was built to prove that powered flight is possible
    in the thin air of Mars.
  solarPanelNarrationText: Two rotors, 1.2 meters across, spin in opposite directions
    about 2,400 times a minute to lift Ingenuity in the thin Martian air.
  cameraMastNarrationText: The solar panel on top charges the batteries that power
    each flight and keep Ingenuity warm through the freezing nights.
  instrumentArmNarrationText: Four light, springy legs let Ingenuity touch down softly
    after each flight.
  systemsCheckNarrationText: Rotors, power and landing legs are accounted for. Ingenuity
    is ready for launch.
